# Per-Dockerfile ignore file — governs ONLY builds run with `-f Dockerfile.mock`
# (BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` and then does NOT read the
# shared `.dockerignore`). That is why this file exists: the shared file is
# hub-shaped and excludes `mushpi-mock/` — the sole build input of this image.
# It cannot stay hub-lean AND feed this build, so this build gets its own list.
# Everything below is excluded from the context upload; the Dockerfile COPYs
# only pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md, LICENSE and src/ from mushpi-mock/.

# VCS
.git
**/.git

# Sibling repos that are never inputs to THIS image (they may sit in the local
# context as transient clones; per REFERENCE.md they are never vendored).
mushpi-server
mushpi-client
mushpi-grow

# Python scratch a local mushpi-mock clone carries — never build inputs.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# The mock clone's local runtime config — untracked, may hold a real secret.
mushpi-mock/config.json

# Secrets and live state — must never be baked into any image.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
.demo-mock-config.json
data
data-test
mushpi-data
mushpi-demo-data
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Packaging-layer files irrelevant to this build (root-level matches only).
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
.github
release.json
README.md
LICENSE
AGENTS.md
REFERENCE.md
DEPLOYMENT.md
MAINTAINING.md

# Node leftovers — a maintainer's context can carry them; not baked here.
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage

# IDE / hooks
.vscode
.idea
.husky
